    <skos:skos_definition rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A model that incorporates vision capabilities into large language models, often using CAD models or vision encoders to process visual data alongside text.</skos:skos_definition>
    <hasCQ rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0119</hasCQ>
    <prov:wasDerivedFrom rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CQ_S0_R1_0119</prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2305.15964_rag::chunk_004</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2306.00890_rag::chunk_007</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To enhance the vision capability of LLMs, multiple CAD models are incorporated.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">the vision encoder from BioMedCLIP [ 49 ], or initialize the language model from Vicuna [ 43 ], which may lead to higher performance.</hasEvidenceText>
